Package: VaSSTra
Title: Simple Variables to States to Sequences to Trajectories
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Mohammed", "Saqr",
           email = "saqr@saqr.me",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Sonsoles", "López-Pernas", role = "aut")
    )
Description: A small, pipe-friendly implementation of the VaSSTra workflow
    for longitudinal multivariate data. It provides explicit steps to turn
    variables into states, states into aligned sequences, and sequences into
    trajectory groups, followed by tidy trajectory descriptions. A single
    call runs the complete analysis with transparent, overridable automation
    of data roles and cluster counts, and an evaluation verb compares the
    fitted clustering against its alternatives. 'Nestimate' provides the
    default sequence-clustering backend and all sequence plots. No
    'TraMineR' dependency is required.
